§ `reg. 3 -- the annual indexation of the fees`

-- reg. 3(a): the reg. 2 amounts are updated on 1 January of each year by the
-- rate of change of the new index against the base index, and rounded to the
-- nearest whole new shekel. The rounding of an exact half is not settled by the
-- text; half-up is the reading adopted. The fees are the five distinct amounts
-- that appear across the texts of reg. 2 -- the two enacted vintages and the
-- never-enacted draft: 40, 158, 194, 284 and 398.

-- Ordinary movements of the index, across all five fee amounts.

-- new index 100 against base index 100 -- no change: the index stood still.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 40 100 100 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 158 100 100 EQUALS 158
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 194 100 100 EQUALS 194
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 284 100 100 EQUALS 284
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 398 100 100 EQUALS 398

-- new index 105.3 against base index 104.1 -- a small rise, the pair used in the encoding's own illustrations.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 40 105.3 104.1 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 158 105.3 104.1 EQUALS 160
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 194 105.3 104.1 EQUALS 196
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 284 105.3 104.1 EQUALS 287
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 398 105.3 104.1 EQUALS 403

-- new index 112.4 against base index 100 -- a larger rise.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 40 112.4 100 EQUALS 45
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 158 112.4 100 EQUALS 178
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 194 112.4 100 EQUALS 218
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 284 112.4 100 EQUALS 319
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 398 112.4 100 EQUALS 447

-- new index 99.2 against base index 101.5 -- a fall: the updated fee goes down.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 40 99.2 101.5 EQUALS 39
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 158 99.2 101.5 EQUALS 154
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 194 99.2 101.5 EQUALS 190
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 284 99.2 101.5 EQUALS 278
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 398 99.2 101.5 EQUALS 389

-- new index 101 against base index 100 -- a rise of one per cent.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 40 101 100 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 158 101 100 EQUALS 160
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 194 101 100 EQUALS 196
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 284 101 100 EQUALS 287
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 398 101 100 EQUALS 402

-- Exactly on the half. Each pair below is engineered so that the product
-- fee x new / base is a whole number of shekels plus exactly one half, which
-- is where half-up, half-even and truncation part company. Half-up rounds
-- every one of them away from zero.

-- 40 x 81 / 80 = 40.5 exactly -- just above par.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 40 81 80 EQUALS 41
-- 40 x 83 / 80 = 41.5 exactly -- a three per cent rise.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 40 83 80 EQUALS 42
-- 40 x 77 / 80 = 38.5 exactly -- a three per cent fall.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 40 77 80 EQUALS 39

-- 158 x 317 / 316 = 158.5 exactly -- just above par.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 158 317 316 EQUALS 159
-- 158 x 325 / 316 = 162.5 exactly -- a three per cent rise.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 158 325 316 EQUALS 163
-- 158 x 307 / 316 = 153.5 exactly -- a three per cent fall.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 158 307 316 EQUALS 154

-- 194 x 389 / 388 = 194.5 exactly -- just above par.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 194 389 388 EQUALS 195
-- 194 x 399 / 388 = 199.5 exactly -- a three per cent rise.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 194 399 388 EQUALS 200
-- 194 x 377 / 388 = 188.5 exactly -- a three per cent fall.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 194 377 388 EQUALS 189

-- 284 x 569 / 568 = 284.5 exactly -- just above par.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 284 569 568 EQUALS 285
-- 284 x 585 / 568 = 292.5 exactly -- a three per cent rise.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 284 585 568 EQUALS 293
-- 284 x 551 / 568 = 275.5 exactly -- a three per cent fall.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 284 551 568 EQUALS 276

-- 398 x 797 / 796 = 398.5 exactly -- just above par.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 398 797 796 EQUALS 399
-- 398 x 819 / 796 = 409.5 exactly -- a three per cent rise.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 398 819 796 EQUALS 410
-- 398 x 773 / 796 = 386.5 exactly -- a three per cent fall.
#ASSERT `the updated fee` 398 773 796 EQUALS 387

§ `s.8 -- the period of validity of a licence`

-- s.8: a licence is valid for five years, or until 31 March of the fifth year
-- from the year in which it was granted, whichever is the earlier. So a licence
-- granted after 31 March is cut short by the 31 March cap, and one granted on or
-- before it runs its full five years. The fifth year from the grant year is read
-- as grant year + 5.

-- Granted in 2025. The cap falls on 31 March 2030.
#ASSERT `the licence expires on` (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 1   -- five years
#ASSERT `the licence expires on` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15   -- five years
#ASSERT `the licence expires on` (YMD 2025 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2030 2 28   -- five years
#ASSERT `the licence expires on` (YMD 2025 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31   -- the 31 March cap
#ASSERT `the licence expires on` (YMD 2025 4 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31   -- the 31 March cap
#ASSERT `the licence expires on` (YMD 2025 6 30) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31   -- the 31 March cap
#ASSERT `the licence expires on` (YMD 2025 9 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31   -- the 31 March cap
