§ `s.63 -- commencement`

-- s.63(a)(1): for systems using a flammable refrigerant, the Law commences three
-- months from its publication or on the commencement of the fee regulations under
-- s.59, whichever is the later -- and that day is 'the commencement day'.
-- s.63(a)(2): for a system on a refrigerant outside the Fourth Schedule, eighteen months from the commencement day.
-- Both periods are month arithmetic, so both clamp to the length of the month
-- they land in.

-- s.63(a)(1): the later of three months from publication and the fee
-- regulations coming into force.

-- What actually happened: published 14 january 2025, the fee regulations in force from 16 july 2025, which is the later.
#ASSERT `the commencement day` (YMD 2025 1 14) (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16

-- The counterfactual: had the fee regulations come into force on 1 march 2025, three months from publication would have been the later.
#ASSERT `the commencement day` (YMD 2025 1 14) (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 14

-- The tie: the fee regulations in force on the very day three months from publication falls.
#ASSERT `the commencement day` (YMD 2025 1 14) (YMD 2025 4 14) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 14

-- A month-end clamp: 30 november plus three months is 28 february, there being no 30 february.
#ASSERT `the commencement day` (YMD 2025 11 30) (YMD 2025 12 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28

-- The same clamp in a leap year: 29 february 2028.
#ASSERT `the commencement day` (YMD 2027 11 30) (YMD 2028 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29

-- 31 january plus three months is 30 april, april being a thirty-day month.
#ASSERT `the commencement day` (YMD 2025 1 31) (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 30

-- 31 august plus three months is 30 november.
#ASSERT `the commencement day` (YMD 2025 8 31) (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 11 30

-- 30 november 2024 plus three months is 28 february 2025, which is not a leap year.
#ASSERT `the commencement day` (YMD 2024 11 30) (YMD 2024 12 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28

-- s.63(a)(2): eighteen months from the commencement day.

-- The real commencement day.
#ASSERT `the Law applies to systems on refrigerants outside the Fourth Schedule from` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16

-- The counterfactual commencement day.
#ASSERT `the Law applies to systems on refrigerants outside the Fourth Schedule from` (YMD 2025 4 14) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 14

-- An ordinary 28 february.
#ASSERT `the Law applies to systems on refrigerants outside the Fourth Schedule from` (YMD 2026 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2027 8 28

-- A leap day: august has thirty-one days, so nothing is clamped.
#ASSERT `the Law applies to systems on refrigerants outside the Fourth Schedule from` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2029 8 29

-- 31 august plus eighteen months is clamped to 28 february 2027.
#ASSERT `the Law applies to systems on refrigerants outside the Fourth Schedule from` (YMD 2025 8 31) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28

-- The same clamp landing in a leap year: 29 february 2028.
#ASSERT `the Law applies to systems on refrigerants outside the Fourth Schedule from` (YMD 2026 8 31) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29

-- 31 december plus eighteen months is clamped to 30 june.
#ASSERT `the Law applies to systems on refrigerants outside the Fourth Schedule from` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2027 6 30

-- 31 march plus eighteen months is clamped to 30 september.
#ASSERT `the Law applies to systems on refrigerants outside the Fourth Schedule from` (YMD 2025 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 30

§ `ss.2 and 3 -- the grades and the duty to hold a licence`

-- s.2: a Grade 1 licence reaches a system of up to 18 kW, a Grade 2 licence up to
-- 70 kW, and a Grade 3 licence any system. s.3(a): a person shall not perform the
-- work unless holding a licence of the type suited to that system. s.3(b): the
-- Minister may exempt types of system by order, and an exempted system needs no
-- licence at all. The cooling outputs below sit on both sides of each ceiling,
-- a hundredth of a kilowatt apart, because 'up to' includes the ceiling itself.

-- The lowest grade that may work on a system of the stated output.
#ASSERT `the lowest grade permitted to work on a system of` 0 EQUALS `Grade 1`
#ASSERT `the lowest grade permitted to work on a system of` 1 EQUALS `Grade 1`
#ASSERT `the lowest grade permitted to work on a system of` 17.99 EQUALS `Grade 1`
#ASSERT `the lowest grade permitted to work on a system of` 18 EQUALS `Grade 1`
#ASSERT `the lowest grade permitted to work on a system of` 18.01 EQUALS `Grade 2`
#ASSERT `the lowest grade permitted to work on a system of` 50 EQUALS `Grade 2`
#ASSERT `the lowest grade permitted to work on a system of` 69.99 EQUALS `Grade 2`
#ASSERT `the lowest grade permitted to work on a system of` 70 EQUALS `Grade 2`
#ASSERT `the lowest grade permitted to work on a system of` 70.01 EQUALS `Grade 3`
#ASSERT `the lowest grade permitted to work on a system of` 100 EQUALS `Grade 3`
#ASSERT `the lowest grade permitted to work on a system of` 1000 EQUALS `Grade 3`

-- A licence holder, on a system that has not been exempted by order. A
-- licence of a higher grade reaches down to the smaller systems as well.

-- A Grade 1 licence.
#ASSERT `the licence grade reaches the system` (JUST `Grade 1`) 0 FALSE
#ASSERT `the licence grade reaches the system` (JUST `Grade 1`) 1 FALSE
#ASSERT `the licence grade reaches the system` (JUST `Grade 1`) 17.99 FALSE
